<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leonardo Alagon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1436–<a href="/years/1494">1494</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Leonardo de Alagón</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leonardo Alagon was Marquis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oristano">Oristano</a>, heir through his mother to the old Judicate of Arborea in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>. Quarrelling with the Aragonese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>, he rose in revolt in the 1470s and won early successes, but was defeated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-macomer">Battle of Macomer</a> in 1478. Captured, he spent the rest of his life imprisoned in the castle of Xàtiva in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and his marquisate passed to the crown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leonardo-alagon.jpg" alt="Leonardo Alagon" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leonardo_Alagon,_marchese_di_Oristano.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
